<given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bach</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Syngeneic transfer of autoimmune diabetes from diabetic NOD  mice to healthy neonates. Requirement for both L3T4<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> and  Lyt-2<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>T cells</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1987</year><volume>166</volume><fpage>823</fpage><lpage>832</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Appel</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>O'Neil</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wicker</surname><given-names>LS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Both the Lyt-2<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> and L3T4<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>T cell subsets are required for the transfer of diabetes in nonobese diabetic mice</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><year>1988</year><volume>140</volume><fpage>52</fpage><lpage>58</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haskins</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>McDuffie</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acceleration of diabetes in young NOD mice with a CD4<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>islet-specific T cell clone</article-title><source>Science (Wash DC)</source><year>1990</year><volume>249</volume><fpage>1433</fpage><lpage>1436</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2205920</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wong</surname><given-names>FS</given-names></name><name><surname>Visintin</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Wen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Flavell</surname>